  "id": "racial-socialization",
  "term": "racial socialization",
  "definition": "Racial socialization is the set of messages people receive about race or ethnicity, such as learning about their culture, being prepared for racial bias, or being encouraged to be wary of others. In this context, it refers to how these messages may relate to coping with racism and well-being.",
